  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1212" flags="0x0">
    <title>Steering Damper :: Output compensation (vs 0xFEBF643C, axis unverified)</title>
    <description>Electronic steering damper output-compensation gain (5-pt, centred on 0x8000 = 1.0; stock 1.17 at low end -&gt; 0.88 at high end). Indexed by 0xFEBF643C, an IMU/chassis-derived signed signal (0x8000 = neutral, rate-limited) from the fef0265A-2668 block that also feeds the damper secondary inputs 0xFEBF642A/C/E - i.e. the ESD modulates on vehicle attitude/dynamics, not just speed (exact IMU axis not yet pinned). SHARED within the ESD subsystem: the controller FUN_00078308 multiplies the damper modulation by this gain, and the damper solenoid DIAGNOSTIC (FUN_0003a062 / 0003a0be / 0003a1b6 / 0003a32e, which set fault bits in fef009c9 / fef009ca from the damper command 0xFEBF62BC) scales its expected-feedback thresholds by it. Not shared with any non-damper module.

PORTED FROM HAYABUSA 5JCZSJ10 (HIGH: breakpoints byte-identical, almost certainly the same map). Units/scaling carried over; GSX-R addresses &amp; values are this read's own. Hayabusa code refs are not verified on GSX-R.
